= Meeting with a Bulgarian delegation

After fourteen days of travel around our country, a delegation from the People's Republic of Bulgaria has arrived to the Prague Castle to visit President Novotný. Led by Sava Ganovski, the chairman of the National Assembly of Bulgaria, the delegation seeks discussion about the future developments of a socialist society.

This could be a good opportunity to bolster relations between both countries. However, we need to keep in mind that Bulgaria is one of the more conservative members of the Warsaw Pact, very loyal to the Soviet Union.

@1966_05_01_bd

- @1966_05_01_bd_loyalty: Reassert out commitment to socialism.
- @1966_05_01_bd_vratsa: Mention the recent dam disaster in Vratsa.
- @1966_05_01_bd_end: End the meeting.

@1966_05_01_bd_loyalty
